# Kubernetes Node.js Demo Application

A simple Node.js web application deployed on a local **Kubernetes Kind cluster** using **Nginx Ingress** and optional TLS support.

## 🚀 Features

* Containerized Node.js application (Docker)
* Kubernetes Deployments & Services
* Ingress for external access
* **Optional** TLS termination support
* Local cluster setup using **Kind**

---

## 📁 Project Structure

```
k8s-node-demo/
├── app/
│   ├── server.js
│   ├── package.json
│   └── Dockerfile
├── k8s/
│   ├── namespace.yaml
│   ├── deployment.yaml
│   ├── service.yaml
│   └── ingress.yaml
└── README.md
```

---

## 🏗️ Build and Push Docker Image

```bash
docker build -t <your-dockerhub-username>/node-demo:latest ./app
docker push <your-dockerhub-username>/node-demo:latest
```

---

## 🧱 Create Kubernetes Namespace

```bash
kubectl apply -f k8s/namespace.yaml
```

---

## 🚢 Deploy Application

```bash
kubectl apply -f k8s/deployment.yaml
kubectl apply -f k8s/service.yaml
kubectl apply -f k8s/ingress.yaml
```

---

## 🌍 Access the App

After deployment, access the app via:

```
http://node-demo.local
```

If using Windows, ensure `/etc/hosts` (or Windows hosts file) contains:

```
127.0.0.1 node-demo.local
```

---

## 🔐 (Optional) Enable TLS

```
# Create directory for certs
mkdir certs

# Generate self‑signed certificate
openssl req -x509 -nodes -days 365 -newkey rsa:2048 \
  -keyout certs/node-demo.key \
  -out certs/node-demo.crt \
  -subj "/CN=node-demo.local"

# Create Kubernetes secret
kubectl create secret tls node-demo-tls \
  --namespace demo-app \
  --key certs/node-demo.key \
  --cert certs/node-demo.crt
```

Then update `ingress.yaml` to enable TLS.

---

## ✅ Verify Deployment

```
kubectl get all -n demo-app
```

